user.js
*.mp3
# Compiled bytecode is a build artefact, not source: a committed .pyc ships a binary and
# looks runnable to a reviewer while being impossible to review.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# The prefix can be this checkout (`HERMES_FACE_PREFIX=$PWD`), and then the bridge writes his
# config, his conversation history, the socket token and his speech straight into the tree. None
# of that is source, and the token least of all. Root-anchored so `face/web/presets.json`, which
# is the shipped preset library, stays tracked.
/config.json
/history.json
/presets.json
/token
/audio/
/*.json.tmp
